blurb: |
  <p>confused why someone would throw it in a dumpster.
  I quickily found out that it's because the aluminum seatpost was seized solid in the steel.
  After several failed attempts I used the nuclear option of dissolving it with sodium hydroxide (lye).
  Once I finished ruining the paint job I took it to Pikes Powdercoat to give it a classy hunter green finish.
  A nice clean look if I say so myself. </p>

  <p></p>I swapped out the old tires for a pair of fast rolling Schwalbe Billy Bonkers, perfect for zipping around Boston.
  A Brooks B17 saddle provides, the perfect all weather saddle. The 1x10 drivetrain is simple and reliable for any type of riding.</p>
